  "body": "#2496: `detect_holes` on a Drill op took holes wider than the drill. `generate` and `verify` then passed with no warning, and `post` wrote the program. Each such hole is drilled at the drill diameter, so it comes out undersize. Nothing told the user.\n\nThe fix follows the triage on the issue: name each hole that the drill does not make at its size. A pilot drill stays possible, so the post is not held.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **The law** (new `crates/app/src/operation/drill_size.rs`): `undersize_holes` gives each Z hole wider than the Drill-kind tool by more than `DRILL_SIZE_TOL` (0.1 mm on the diameter).\n  - It reads only cycles that drill to size: Auto, Drill, Peck and Ream. Spot, Tap, FloatingTap, Bore and BackBore size the hole another way.\n  - It reads only the mill's Z holes, not the turret's radial list.\n  - A NaN or infinite hole radius, or a bad tool diameter, names nothing and does not panic.\n- **Detect holes** keeps each such hole and names it in the new `DetectedHoles::undersize` list. Example: `the 8.000 mm hole at (-50.000, 0.000) is wider than the 6.000 mm drill: it is drilled 6.000 mm (a pilot) - use a 8.000 mm drill, or follow with a Bore or a reamer`.\n  - MCP `detect_holes` answers it as `undersize`, beside `skipped`.\n  - The GUI status line shows it. The GUI's pending command field `skipped` is now `notes`, with the skipped and the undersize sentences.\n- **Generate** adds a new advisory `Warning::DrillUndersize { at, hole_mm, drill_mm }` (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`) for each such hole, at its first cutting move.\n  - `blocks_post()` is false, as for `Scallop`, `ProbeSearch` and `SinkerFinishOrder`.\n  - MCP finding kind: `drill_undersize`.\n  - The UI warning list groups it on its own line (key 216). `warned_moves` frames its move.\n- The MCP tool description of `detect_holes` names `undersize` and `drill_undersize`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2496-drill-undersize.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The issue's reproduction (D6, D8 and D12 through holes, catalog `DR-0600`) on a synthetic plate:\n  - `detect_holes`: `holes: 3`, `skipped: []`, and `undersize` names the D8 and the D12 holes.\n  - `generate`: `ok`, with two `drill_undersize` findings, `blocks_post: false`.\n  - `verify`: `ok: true`. `post` writes the program.\n- A D5 hole under the D6 drill: `verify` gives `ok: false` with a blocking `gouge`. The hole-wall excuse is capped at the facet sagitta (`WALL_SAG`, 0.05 mm), so it does not hide that cut. This law does not name it.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/drill_undersize.rs` (new, MCP):\n  - `holes_wider_than_the_drill_are_named_at_detect_and_on_the_path_and_the_post_writes`\n  - `a_hole_at_the_drills_own_size_names_nothing`\n  - `a_hole_narrower_than_the_drill_is_held_as_a_gouge_not_named_undersize`\n- `app::operation::drill_size::tests` (4): the size band (D6.04 and D6.1 are the drill's size, D6.2 and D8 are not), the narrower hole, the cycles and tool kinds that the law does not read, and the bad numbers.\n- `ui::detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_drill_op_keeps_a_wider_hole_and_names_it_undersize`: the GUI status line.\n- Mutation check: with the generate hook removed, the first MCP test fails (`one warning per undersize hole: []`).\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (325 steps, 23 min) ran on the first version, with a 0.05 mm band. 319 steps were green. 6 failed:\n  - `drilling_axial::an_axial_drill_runs_clean_on_the_lathe_and_posts_its_cycle`: from this change. Its \"matched\" fixture has a 4 mm drill in a 4.1 mm hole, and the 0.05 mm band named it. The band is now 0.1 mm (5b16ed7e4), and the suite is green. A wider band names fewer holes, so it cannot make the 319 green steps fail.\n  - `example_catalog` (2 tests), `first_part_programs` (2 tests), `microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a`, `stock_source_holes::framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` and `wire_taper_angle::an_incomplete_dialect_and_a_four_axis_angle_cut_are_refused_by_name`: not from this change. They fail the same way, at the same lines, on a clean worktree of the same base (bd0400ebb) on this Windows machine. `example_catalog` compares an LF program with the committed file read back with CRLF.\n- On 5b16ed7e4: `drill_size` (4), `drill_undersize` (3), `drilling_axial` (7) and the GUI `detect_holes` tests (4): green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: one error, at `crates/app/src/operation/heights.rs:128`. That is #2479 (Clippy 1.99), in a file that this PR does not change. With only that lint allowed (`-A clippy::needless_borrows_for_generic_args`): clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The turret's radial holes (`cross`). The law does not read them.\n- The real STEP file of the issue. The test uses a synthetic STL plate with the same hole sizes.\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\nChangelog: A Drill operation names each hole wider than its drill, at Detect holes and as a warning on the toolpath that does not hold the post (a pilot drill stays possible) (#2496)\n\nEffort: high (the label of the issue). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #2496\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
